00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:55.000
bank, while he collected the hall from the safe and vault. They just needed one more person. Helms had the perfect man for the job, another ex-con who was experienced with firearms. Although the men didn't plan on shooting anybody, they wanted to appear as though they knew what they were doing when carrying their weapons. As their chosen date approached, the would-be fourth member of the crew became bedridden with the flu. Helms and Hill took this as an omen, suggesting they delayed the robbery until the new year, but Ratliff was adamant, as he had determined that the bank would contain the most money on the last Friday before it closed for Christmas. Helms suggested his in-law, Louis Davis, might fit the bill. Davis had never been

