39
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:56.000
discovering Lewis Davis bleeding in the back seat. Officer Reddys decided to call off the police pursuit to tend to the traumatized Harris family and to place Davis under arrest. Davis was taken to Fort Worth Hospital and placed by the window in a ground floor room as crowds gathered to gawk at him. When he regained consciousness, the police demanded he reveal the names of his accomplices, warning he would be put to death in the electric chair otherwise, but Davis remained tight-lipped. Several armed citizens continued to chase after the Buick, prompting Ratliff, Helms and Hill to throw roofing nails out the car window to puncture

